# UniCar documentation

This directory contains a written record of the UniCar undergraduate project. The notes were organized after the TCC and should be read together with the final academic report.

## Original project

UniCar was an Android prototype built by Leonardo Henrique Oliveira and Bruna Helena Antonialli Gomes with MIT App Inventor, Firebase Authentication, Firebase Realtime Database and TinyDB. The final report contains the original interface screenshots and programming blocks.

The original App Inventor project file and image assets are not currently included in this repository. This documentation does not recreate or replace those artifacts.

## Documents in this directory

- `academic-context`: authorship, academic scope and repository limitations
- `overview`: short description of the problem and prototype
- `features`: functions demonstrated in the academic prototype
- `user-flow`: login, ride offer, ride request and contact flows
- `business-rules`: rules described for users, offers and available seats
- `data-model`: how Firebase and TinyDB were used
- `architecture`: original App Inventor-based organization
- `technical-decisions.md`: reasons for the main technology choices

## Later Python exercise

The repository root also contains `core_python/`. That directory was created later by Leonardo as a programming exercise based on a subset of the same domain. It is not the source code of UniCar, was not part of the submitted TCC and should not be attributed to both original authors.

## Separate project

Smart Carpool is a different web portfolio project. The two projects share a subject area, but not source code, interface, architecture or Git history.
